    <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">Frequently asked questions</p>
    <h1>Your questions, answered</h1>
    <p class="lead">Everything you need to know before your voyage to the Palomino Islands.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="accordion">
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">1.</span> How long is the tour<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">The Palomino Islands tour lasts approximately <strong>3.5 hours</strong>.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">2.</span> What are the yachts like<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Our yachts are <strong>two-deck</strong> vessels, with a lounge/dining area, a galley and two cabins to change into swimwear. Each vessel has two restrooms.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">3.</span> What does the trip include<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Bilingual guide, life vest, a stop to swim with the sea lions, and a service of sodas, hot drinks (tea, chamomile, anise) and light snacks (crisps, plantain chips, pretzels) — <strong>unlimited</strong>. Wetsuits with limited stock in the cold season. <a href="/en/tour/">See everything included →</a></div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">4.</span> Can babies travel<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">There is no age limit: even babies can travel.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">5.</span> Can older adults travel<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, as long as they are in good health.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">6.</span> Where is the boarding point<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">We board from a <strong>private pier in La Punta, Callao</strong>. The exact address is given when you book.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">7.</span> Is there safe parking<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, the La Punta municipal public car park has permanent security.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">8.</span> Can people with disabilities travel<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">It depends on the type of disability. Write to us and we'll review it with you.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">9.</span> Is there a restroom<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, each vessel has two restrooms.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">10.</span> What should I wear<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Sportswear according to the season, plus a warm layer.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">11.</span> Does the tour have a guide<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, we have a <strong>bilingual English–Spanish</strong> tourism guide.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">12.</span> Is there travel insurance<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, all passengers are insured.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">13.</span> Can I enter the sea if I can't swim<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, you can enter the sea wearing a <strong>life vest</strong>.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">14.</span> Could I get seasick<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Following our recommendations, it is unlikely you'll get seasick.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">15.</span> How long can I swim with the sea lions<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">On average <strong>30 to 40 minutes</strong>.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">16.</span> Do you lend wetsuits<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, we have a limited stock that we use in winter.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">17.</span> How do I book<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">From the <a href="/en/contacto/">Contact</a> section of this site, or by phone at <strong>{{ site.phone }}</strong>, providing the passenger list: full names, ages, ID number (DNI, passport or foreigner's card) and a contact mobile number.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">18.</span> Can I shower inside the yacht<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">We have a handheld shower you can use after swimming with the sea lions. Shampoo and soap aren't allowed; it's only for rinsing off.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">19.</span> Do you give seasickness tablets<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes, one tablet per passenger is provided at the start of the trip. It's completely free.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">20.</span> Are seats numbered<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">No, seats are not numbered. You can move around any area of the yacht, on the first and second decks.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">21.</span> Do the sea lions bite<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">The sea lions don't bite. You'll swim with the baby sea lions, which are playful and curious; the adults always stay on the island.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">22.</span> Is the sea very cold<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">In summer the water isn't very cold and you can swim in swimwear. In winter it's colder, so we lend wetsuits to swim with the sea lions.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">23.</span> Are photos included<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">We don't include a photo service, but our crew can help you with your phone or camera.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">24.</span> Can I bring food<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">Yes. We recommend something light, as eating too much at sea can cause seasickness.</div></details>
      <details><summary><span class="q-no">25.</span> Can I pay on the day of the tour<b>?</b></summary><div class="answer">No, payment is always in advance. You can pay at our office (Av. Arequipa 4964, Of. 202, Miraflores), by bank transfer or deposit (ask for the account numbers when booking), or at the <strong>Tu Entrada</strong> points of sale in Plaza Vea or Vivanda, with prior reservation.</div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
